        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.046,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Proportional Reasoning-1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "separates two rooms. To build a wall of 10-feet, he requires approximately 1450 bricks. How many bricks would he need to build the house? Assume all walls are of the same height and thickness."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.158,
            0.711,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.416,
            0.803,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": "？ Puneeth’s father went from Lucknow to Kanpur in 2 hours by riding his motorcycle at a speed of 50 km/h. If he drives at 75 km/h, how long will it take him to reach Kanpur? Can we form this problem as a proportion—"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.416,
            0.905,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.427,
            0.497,
            0.546,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": "50:2:75:",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.521,
            0.847,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "Would it take Puneeth’s father more time or less time to reach Kanpur? Think about it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.558,
            0.761,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": "Even though this problem looks similar to the previous problems, it cannot be solved using the Rule of Three!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.595,
            0.761,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "The time of travel would actually decrease when the speed increases. So this problem cannot be modelled as 50 : 2 :: 75 : \\_\\_."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.772,
            0.547,
            0.879,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.644,
            0.848,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "？ **Activity 2:** Go to the market and collect the prices of different sizes of shampoo containers of the same shampoo and create a table like the one given below. See if the volume of shampoo is proportional to the price."
        },
        {
